    "title": "OSU players say Tulsa loss helped team not look ahead - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Cayden Cox, Assistant Sports Editor, @cayden_cox05 ,\n1 hours ago James Williams said it best. Oklahoma State has to take it one game at a time. “I mean, we lost to Tulsa,” Williams said. “Everything’s in front of us. We’re not thinking, ‘oh, we beat Oregon so everything else is great.’ I’m actually glad that happened to us. It’ll keep us humble for the rest of the season, especially as we begin Big 12 play.” Read full article",
